dce43e5"} {"question" "q-104925" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5d3e201778a4c3fe75f10c5cc7b701c5453a3e60021b05eb3f9f7bced8a7aad2"} {"question" "q-104925" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-104925" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{-1},{0,1}"] ["math" "{0},{-1},{1},{-1,1}"] ["math" "{0},{1},{-1,0}"] ["math" "∅,{0},{1},{0,1}"] ["math" "∅,{1},{1,2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-104925" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "∅,{0},{1},{0,1}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-80812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are subsets of ${Q}^{+}$  (the set of positive rational numbers)?\n\n- ${Q}_{0}^{+}$ (the set of non-negative rational numbers)\n- $N$\n- $Z$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-80812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "$A$ is a subset of $B$ if every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect the given choices.\n\n- ${Q}_{0}^{+}$ is not a subset of ${Q}^{+}.$ For example, $0\\in {Q}_{0}^{+}$ but $0\\notin {Q}^{+}.$\n\n- $N$ is a subset of ${Q}^{+}.$ Indeed, every natural number is also a positive rational number.\n\n- $Z$ is not a subset of ${Q}^{+}.$ For example, $-1\\in Z$ but $-1\\notin {Q}^{+}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-80812" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5d3e201778a4c3fe75f10c5cc7b701c5453a3e60021b05eb3f9f7bced8a7aad2"} {"question" "q-80812" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-80812" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-80812" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-80810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which statement is **not** true?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-80810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $A⊆B,$ then $A$ is a subset of $B,$ meaning that every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nAmong the given choices, only $Z⊆N$ is not true. This statement is not true because not every integer is a natural number.  For example, we have $-1\\in Z$ but $-1\\notin N.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-80810" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5d3e201778a4c3fe75f10c5cc7b701c5453a3e60021b05eb3f9f7bced8a7aad2"} {"question" "q-80810" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-80810" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "N⊆C"] ["math" "N⊆Q"] ["math" "Q⊆R"] ["math" "Z⊆N"] ["math" "Z⊆R"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-80810" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "Z⊆N"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are subsets of $R?$\n\n- ${Q}^{+}$ (the set of positive rationals)\n- ${Z}^{-}$ (the set of negative integers)\n- $N$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "$A$ is a subset of $B$ if every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect the given choices.\n\n- ${Q}^{+}$ is  a subset of $R.$ Every positive rational number is a real number.\n\n- ${Z}^{-}$ is a subset of $R.$ Every negative integer number is a real number.\n\n- $N$ a subset of $R.$ Every natural number is a real number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5d3e201778a4c3fe75f10c5cc7b701c5453a3e60021b05eb3f9f7bced8a7aad2"} {"question" "q-506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-506" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and III"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-105039" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which statement is **not** true?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-105039" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If $A⊆B,$ then $A$ is a subset of $B,$ meaning that every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nAmong the given choices, only ${Z}^{-}⊆N$ is not true. This statement is not true because not every negative integer is a natural number. For example, we have $-1\\in {Z}^{-}$ but $-1\\notin N.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-105039" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5d3e201778a4c3fe75f10c5cc7b701c5453a3e60021b05eb3f9f7bced8a7aad2"} {"question" "q-105039" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-105039" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "N⊆C"] ["math" "Q⊆Q"] ["math" "Q⊆R"] ["math" "Z⊆Q"] ["math" "{Z}^{-}⊆N"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-105039" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{Z}^{-}⊆N"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-105034" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are subsets of $R?$\n\n- ${Q}^{-}$ (the set of negative rationals)\n- ${Z}^{+}$ (the set of positive integers)\n- $N$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-105034" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "$A$ is a subset of $B$ if every element of $A$ is an element of $B.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect the given choices.\n\n- ${Q}^{-}$ is  a subset of $R.$ Every negative rational number is a real number.\n\n- ${Z}^{+}$ is a subset of $R.$ Every positive integer number is a real number.\n\n- $N$ a subset of $R.$ Every natural number is a real number.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II and III\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-105034" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5d3e201778a4c3fe75f10c5cc7b701c5453a3e60021b05eb3f9f7bced8a7aad2"} {"question" "q-105034" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-105034" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I, II and III"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-105034" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II and III"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-37267" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true for the sets $A={5,10,15,20,25,30,35,…}$ and $B={5n∣n\\in N,3\\le n\\le 7}?$\n\n- $B⊆A$\n- $A⊆B$\n- $A⊈B$\n- $A⊇B$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-37267" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we must find the elements of the set $B.$ Substituting the values $n\\in {3,4,5,6,7}$ into the formula $5n,$ we get the following elements:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n=3 & \\,⇒\\,5(3)=15 \\\\ n=4 & \\,⇒\\,5(4)=20 \\\\ n=5 & \\,⇒\\,5(5)=25 \\\\ n=6 & \\,⇒\\,5(6)=30 \\\\ n=7 & \\,⇒\\,5(7)=35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nB={15,20,25,30,35}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $B⊆A$ is true. Every element in the set $B$ is an element of the set $A.$\n\n- $A⊆B$ is false, while $A⊈B$ is true. For example, $5\\in A$ but $5\\notin B.$\n\n- $A⊇B$ is equivalent to $B⊆A,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, III, and IV only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-37267" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5d3e201778a4c3fe75f10c5cc7b701c5453a3e60021b05eb3f9f7bced8a7aad2"} {"question" "q-37267" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-37267" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I, II, and III only"] ["text" "I, II, and IV only"] ["text" "I, III, and IV only"] ["text" "II and IV only"] ["text" "III and IV only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-37267" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, III, and IV only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-80845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true for the sets $A={n\\in Z∣n+1\\ge -1}$ and $B={n\\in Z∣n-2\\ge -4}?$\n\n- $A⊆B$\n- $B⊆A$\n- $B⊈A$\n- $B⊇A$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-80845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we must find the elements of the sets $A$ and $B.$\n\n- The elements of the set $A$ are all the integer numbers that satisfy the inequality $n+1\\ge -1,$ that is to say, $n\\ge -2.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nA={-2,-1,0,1,2,3,4,5,6,…}.\n$$\n\n- On the other hand, the elements of the set $B$ are all integers that satisfy the inequality $n-2\\ge -4,$ That is to say, $n\\ge -2.$ So, we have \n\n$$\nB={-2,-1,0,1,2,3,4,5,6,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $A⊆B$ is true. Every element in the set $A$ is an element of the set $B.$\n\n- $B⊆A$ is true, while $B⊈A$ is false. Every element in the set $B$ is an element of the set $A.$\n\n- $B⊇A$ is equivalent to $A⊆B,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and IV only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-80845" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5d3e201778a4c3fe75f10c5cc7b701c5453a3e60021b05eb3f9f7bced8a7aad2"} {"question" "q-80845" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-80845" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I, II, and IV only"] ["text" "I, III, and IV only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II and IV only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-80845" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, II, and IV only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-37260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true for the sets $A={x\\in N:3\\le x<9}$ and $B={x\\in N:3x<10}?$\n\n- $A⊆B$\n- $B⊆A$\n- $∅⊆A$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-37260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we must find the elements of the sets $A$ and $B.$\n\n- The elements of the set $A$ are all natural numbers greater than or equal to $3$ but less than $9.$ So,\n\n$$\nA={3,4,5,6,7,8}.\n$$\n\n- On the other hand, the elements of the set $B$ are natural numbers which satisfy the inequality $3x<10.$ So,\n\n$$\nB={1,2,3}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $A⊆B$ is false. For example, $4\\in A$ but $4\\notin B.$\n\n- $B⊆A$ is false. For example, $1\\in B$ but $1\\notin A.$\n\n- $∅⊆A$ is true. The null set $∅={}$ is a subset of *every* set.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-37260" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5d3e201778a4c3fe75f10c5cc7b701c5453a3e60021b05eb3f9f7bced8a7aad2"} {"question" "q-37260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-37260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-37260" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-105064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true for the sets $A={n\\in N∣n-2\\ge 4}$ and $B={n\\in Z∣n+2\\ge 5}?$\n\n- $A⊆B$\n- $B⊆A$\n- $∅⊆A$\n- $B⊇A$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-105064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we must find the elements of the sets $A$ and $B.$\n\n- The elements of the set $A$ are all the natural numbers that satisfy the inequality $n-2\\ge 4,$ that is to say, $n\\ge 6.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nA={6,7,8,9,10,11,…}.\n$$\n\n- On the other hand, the elements of the set $B$ are all integers that satisfy the inequality $n+2\\ge 5,$ That is to say, $n\\ge 3.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nB={3,4,5,6,7,8,…}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $A⊆B$ is true. Every element in the set $A$ is an element of the set $B.$\n\n- $B⊆A$ is false. For example, $3\\in B$ but $3\\notin A.$\n\n- $∅⊆A$ is true. The null set $∅={}$ is a subset of *every* set.\n\n- $B⊇A$ is equivalent to $A⊆B,$ which is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, III, and IV only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-105064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5d3e201778a4c3fe75f10c5cc7b701c5453a3e60021b05eb3f9f7bced8a7aad2"} {"question" "q-105064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-105064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I, II, and IV only"] ["text" "I, III, and IV only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "III and IV only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-105064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I, III, and IV only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-1210" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following statements are true for the sets $A={x\\in Z:-2\\le x<6}$ and $B={x\\in N:x+1<6}?$\n\n- $∅⊆B$\n- $B⊆A$\n- $A⊈B$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-1210" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we must find the elements of the sets $A$ and $B.$\n\n- The elements of the set $A$ are all integer numbers greater than or equal to $-2$ but less than $6.$ So,\n\n$$\nA={-2,-1,0,1,2,3,4,5}.\n$$\n\n- On the other hand, the elements of the set $B$ are natural numbers that satisfy the inequality $x+1<6.$ So,\n\n$$\nB={1,2,3,4}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's inspect the given statements.\n\n- $∅⊆B$ is true. The null set $∅={}$ is a subset of *every* set.\n\n- $B⊆A$ is true. Every element in the set $B$ is an element of the set $A.$\n\n- $A⊈B$ is true. For example, $-1\\in A$ but $-1\\notin B.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-1210" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "5d3e201778a4c3fe75f10c5cc7b701c5453a3e60021b05eb3f9f7bced8a7aad2"} {"question" "q-1210" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038640/state.json" "file_sha256" "7456475955196ab1459228890db2ba1ddd310af4a542545110235036cdce43e5"} {"question" "q-